  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "台灣考古學與原住民",
    "sub_ename": "TAIWANESE ARCHAEOLOGY AND THE INDIGENOUS PEOPLES IN TAIWAN",
    "describe_ch": "理解台灣原住民的歷史文化是理解台灣歷史其中一部分。生活在台灣的原住民先民對於自然環境的知識及利用也可以為氣候變遷所苦的我們作為借鑒。而考古學是認識台灣原住民歷史文化的其中一個學術領域。本課程以考古學的發現研究為基礎介紹台灣的考古遺址及舊石器和新石器文化，並以此理解台灣原住民(平埔族及高山族)的物質文化。此課程也包括參觀遺址、番仔園文化展覽及自然科學博物館的體驗課程以加深對原住民歷史文化的理解。",
    "describe_eh": "Understanding history of Taiwan largely involves in unveiling the history and culture of Taiwanese indigenous peoples. How the ancestors of Taiwanese indigenous peoples adapted to the natural environment and developed the knowledge of their surroundings may be one of the keys to the solutions of climate change and energy management. Through the introduction to the archaeological sites across Taiwan and the material cultures of the prehistoric peoples, we could reconstruct the lifestyles of the peoples and reflect on ours. Visiting an archaeological site located in Taichung, the exhibition of the Fanziyuan Culture and the Liu lab at the National Museum of Natural Science will further broaden our perspective on the history, culture, heritage, and environment of this island.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
